+# REA `execute-rizin-command` on the round-2 PE
+
+## Axes and scope
+
+- **Calibration:** compare the REA envelope, command result, and exit status rather than treating them as interchangeable.
+- **Coverage:** exercise `iI`, `iS`, missing path, directory, unknown command, and semicolon chaining on a real PE; retain one receipt per invocation.
+- **Depth:** preserve both raw command output and typed REA status, including the limits of the generic path errors and the shell-escape safety boundary.
+
+The target is the round-2 setuptools `cli-64.exe` (historical SHA-256 `bbb3de57…`, `corpus/knowledge/2026-10-13-r2-pe-e2e-proof.md:10-15`). Its old cache path was absent during this leg; the selected unblob copy is the same 14,336-byte PE by exact SHA-256 and `file(1)` identity (`.ufo/waves/round-20/evidence/c2/rizin-pe/carrier-identity.md:3-24`). The REA subject envelope independently reports that digest and current local path (`01-iI/stdout.toon:1-8`). Rizin resolved from PATH to `/usr/bin/rizin`, whose local version output is 0.8.2; the REA Evidence field remains `provider.version: null`, so the provider binary is not digest-bound by the Evidence (`carrier-identity.md:26-36`, `01-iI/stdout.toon:9-12`).
+
+All invocations used `npx -y rea-agents@6.5.0 execute-rizin-command`, cwd `/tmp/kr20-KaidokuR20.RizinPeLeg-2`, and no `REA_*` environment variables. The receipts record argv, cwd, REA environment, start/end UTC, exit, selected carrier SHA, actual input path/kind, stdout/stderr path, byte length and SHA-256. All files are below 8 MiB; no xz compression was needed. The original 01–05 output files were restored from immediate replays whose stdout SHA-256 and Evidence IDs matched byte-for-byte; replay receipts 09–13 retain those additional invocations as well.
+
+## Observations
+
